## Interface: 30300
## Title: Demon Hunter
## Notes: Double jump and glide for the Demon Hunter class, plus defensive class-UI constants so party and raid frames survive a Demon Hunter in the group.
## Author: wowserver
## Version: 1.0
## SavedVariables: DemonHunterSaved
## DefaultState: enabled

# Load order matters.
#   Core.lua declares the DemonHunter table, Say(), the saved-variable defaults and the event
#   frame, so it has to come first -- everything below stores itself into that table.
#   ClassUI.lua runs its whole job at load time and is deliberately NOT class-gated: the
#   character who crashes on a missing CLASS_ICON_TCOORDS.DEMONHUNTER is the priest standing
#   next to the Demon Hunter, not the Demon Hunter. See the header of that file.
#   Movement.lua is class-gated and does nothing until Core calls it at PLAYER_LOGIN.
#
# Bindings.xml is deliberately NOT listed: the client loads an addon's Bindings.xml by itself,
# and naming it here would load it twice. (Same rule as ItemBrowser.toc.)
Core.lua
ClassUI.lua
Movement.lua
